ne":null,"start_side":null,"line":2327,"original_line":2327,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1887267396,"original_position":479,"position":479,"subject_type":"line"},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/pulls/27883","id":2209164891,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAA3dP86DrS5b","html_url":"https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/27883","diff_url":"https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/27883.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/27883.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/issues/27883","number":27883,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"MAINT,ENH: Reorganize buffered iteration setup","user":{"login":"seberg","id":61977,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTc3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61977?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seberg","html_url":"https://github.com/seberg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seberg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seberg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seberg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seberg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seberg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seberg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seberg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seberg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seberg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This changes the buffered iteration setup to do most of the work initially rather than when actually copying buffers.

It has a few changes:
- As of now, a very slightly higher overhead initially.
- Shrinks the buffersize to fit the dimensions.  This means that buffers can be re-used far more often for broadcast operations.
  (To be fair, this is most important with reductions where the buffersize always had to be shrunk down.)
- The buffer re-use logic is now passably understandable, I hope.  Which means we may also be able to optimize it further (e.g. allow re-use for dtypes with references, which currently fails...).
- Tries to guess the whether using buffers is actually worthwhile.  And example is:
  ```
  a = np.ones((4, 500))[::2]
  %timeit a + a  # 840ns vs. 1.15
  ```
  so not sure it is important, could maybe safe on it and just grow as much as possible.
  (A possible new optimization: Use "reduce" loop even if not a reduce.)


It still needs:
- [x] Figure out why CI breaks down when local run did not.
- [x] (largely ok) A bit of cleanup (e.g. unnecessary moving around).  The main function is long and a bit messy, I admit.  But a second pair of eyes is probably better at suggesting improvements if they are worthwhile.
- [ ] Someone will probably want some good speedup examples.  They exist, but I need to nail down the nicest ones.
- [x] Decide what to do about `NPY_ITER_CONTIG`.","created_at":"2024-12-01T22:12:59Z","updated_at":"2024-12-16T19:16:29Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"2a4abe605640331d06680cd807ad640c535ee7a6","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":36825825,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNjgyNTgyNQ==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/labels/03%20-%20Maintenance","name":"03 - Maintenance","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":null}],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/pulls/27883/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/pulls/27883/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/issues/27883/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/statuses/1836fd14eba0e0c6466c884c5c8f6ab41392fda4","head":{"label":"seberg:reduce-buf-refactor","ref":"reduce-buf-refactor","sha":"1836fd14eba0e0c6466c884c5c8f6ab41392fda4","user":{"login":"seberg","id":61977,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTc3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61977?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seberg","html_url":"https://github.com/seberg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seberg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seberg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seberg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seberg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seberg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seberg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seberg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seberg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seberg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_a